1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,380
[ELLIOTT]
Blast it!

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,580
Every one of them is drenched!

3
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:05,500
Oh, no.

4
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:07,830
How can this be?

5
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:10,290
The roof's leaking.

6
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:12,790
How did we not notice it?

7
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,960
No one knew
that it would rain so much.

8
00:00:15,330 --> 00:00:17,210
It's unusual
for this time of year.

9
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:20,290
[ANNE]
If it's all ruined,

10
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,630
we won't finish in time
for the festival!

11
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:24,750
[rain falling]

12
00:00:25,210 --> 00:00:27,330
Don't cry,
Miss Head of Artisans.

13
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:29,500
So, what now? [gasps]

14
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:31,790
We will figure something out.

15
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:33,540
[gasps] Right!

16
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,500
[clatters]

17
00:00:38,130 --> 00:00:39,460
Then let's grind it again!

18
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:41,960
First, we'll move
all the silver sugar

19
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,540
into the hearth room
to dry it out!

20
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:45,040
Can someone go
and get the mortars

21
00:00:45,130 --> 00:00:46,000
from the workroom?

22
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:46,920
And quickly!

23
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,210
No matter what, let's be done
by the end of the day!

24
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:50,130
[KING, NADIR, VALENTINE, ORLAND]
Right!

25
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:52,460
[footsteps]

26
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:25,250
[rain falling]

27
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:29,250
[footsteps]

28
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:30,710
The sugar! Is it safe?

29
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,380
[sighs]
It's worse than I feared.

30
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,790
I knew the castle
was damaged in places,

31
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:38,670
but I wasn't expecting all this.

32
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:40,670
You're regrinding it?

33
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,880
I can have my school send more.

34
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,420
Or perhaps
the Radcliffe workshop

35
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,380
could spare some.

36
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:46,710
[ELLIOTT]
Don't be silly,

37
00:02:46,790 --> 00:02:48,130
you know we could never ask
for that.

38
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:50,500
Can you finish then?

39
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,580
I have no doubt.

40
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:56,460
[HUGH]
Good work, everyone!

41
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,540
But tomorrow's the real battle.

42
00:02:58,630 --> 00:02:59,710
Get some rest for now.

43
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,880
♪

44
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:03,880
[sighs]

45
00:03:04,460 --> 00:03:05,960
The rain finally stopped.

46
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,500
Looks that way.

47
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,040
If we give it the whole night
to dry out,

48
00:03:11,130 --> 00:03:12,790
then we can grind some tomorrow.

49
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:15,130
Let me look after the hearth,
all right?

50
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:17,130
Why don't you go
and get some sleep?

51
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:18,630
I can't do that.

52
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:19,880
You should!

53
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:22,290
I wouldn't want
to be ungentlemanlike.

54
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:25,000
Yes,
but I'm the Head of Artisans.

55
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,250
Hm. All right, fine.

56
00:03:27,330 --> 00:03:28,250
We'll take turns.

57
00:03:30,750 --> 00:03:31,670
Do you think...

58
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,130
we can finish everything
before time?

59
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:37,250
[sighs] It's hard to say.

60
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:39,880
Despite what I told
the Viscount,

61
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,540
I'm not all that confident.

62
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:44,040
Even after the silver sugar
is reground,

63
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:45,750
we'll still need time
to create the pieces

64
00:03:45,830 --> 00:03:46,830
and assemble them.

65
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:49,170
If only we had
one more skilled artisan

66
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:50,130
on the team...

67
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:52,130
Do you think Kieth would come
lend us a hand?

68
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:53,920
[ELLIOTT]
Never!

69
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,830
Mr. Radcliffe
wouldn't allow him to.

70
00:03:56,290 --> 00:03:58,500
That's just how tribalism works.

71
00:03:59,130 --> 00:03:59,960
[ANNE sighs]

72
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:02,380
[ANNE] I know,
but there must be someone else!

73
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:05,330
A capable artisan
who doesn't belong to a school.

74
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:08,790
[ANNE, ELLIOTT]
Oh! There's Kat!

75
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,460
[ELLIOTT]
He's in Southcent at the moment,

76
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:13,380
running a shop.

77
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:16,210
I doubt he's got many customers.

78
00:04:16,290 --> 00:04:18,210
If you ask him,
I'm sure he'll help us!

79
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:19,170
[ANNE]
Good!

80
00:04:19,250 --> 00:04:21,170
Then we should all be back
by evening!

81
00:04:21,250 --> 00:04:23,250
And I'll keep an eye on Noah
for you.

82
00:04:23,330 --> 00:04:24,250
[ANNE]
Thank you!

83
00:04:24,710 --> 00:04:26,130
- [CHALLE] Let's go.
- [ANNE] Right!

84
00:04:26,790 --> 00:04:29,790
- [horse neighs]
- [hoofbeats]

85
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:32,710
[sighs]

86
00:04:32,790 --> 00:04:34,130
[footsteps]

87
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:37,040
They're all so cold to you.

88
00:04:37,130 --> 00:04:39,420
Despite how deeply worried
you are for them.

89
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:43,080
I'm used to it, really.

90
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:44,830
[whimpers]

91
00:04:46,290 --> 00:04:48,170
♪

92
00:04:48,250 --> 00:04:51,420
He's never tried very hard
to attract business.

93
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:54,500
[CHALLE] Well,
it's better than last time.

94
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,920
[snoring softly]

95
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,790
- [door creaks]
- [ANNE] Excuse us.

96
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:01,130
- Huh? Uh...
- [door slams]

97
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:03,210
It's good to see you, Benjamin.

98
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:05,500
[BENJAMIN]
That's funny.

99
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,170
You look just like Anne.

100
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:08,130
I am Anne.

101
00:05:08,210 --> 00:05:09,420
It's been a long time.

102
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:11,710
Oh, hello!

103
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:13,880
What brings you
to a place like this?

104
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:16,670
I came to ask something of Kat
if he's here.

105
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:17,750
Is he?

106
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:20,460
Yes, indeed! [grunts]

107
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:24,750
Kat? There's a pretty girl here
to see you!

108
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,250
[door creaks]

109
00:05:26,330 --> 00:05:27,630
Say I'm busy!

110
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:30,210
- Oh, it's you two! Hm.
- [door creaks]

111
00:05:30,290 --> 00:05:31,670
So, you got Challe back?

112
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:34,130
[ANNE] Yes. Thank you so much
for all your help.

113
00:05:34,670 --> 00:05:38,000
There's no need to thank me
since I didn't do anything.

114
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:40,080
Did you come all this way
just to say that?

115
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:42,880
[ANNE] No, actually,
I need a favor.

116
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:43,790
Favor?

117
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:46,040
[ANNE]
Well, currently,

118
00:05:46,130 --> 00:05:47,500
I'm working
as the Head of Artisans

119
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:48,960
at the Paige Workshop.

120
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:50,750
Ooh, how prestigious!

121
00:05:50,830 --> 00:05:52,330
You've really done well!

122
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,330
You see,

123
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,880
we're creating all the pieces

124
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,630
for the Holy Beginnings
Festival.

125
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:59,670
We started working
in Holly Leaf Castle, and then--

126
00:06:00,210 --> 00:06:02,420
I'm familiar with that place, actually.

127
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:03,540
The rain, right?

128
00:06:03,630 --> 00:06:06,130
Yes. The silver sugar's ruined.

129
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:08,170
We're doing our best
to regrind it.

130
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:10,210
But now,
it's put you behind schedule,

131
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:11,830
so you're hoping
I'll lend you a hand

132
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,670
with the sugar confections,
aren't you?

133
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,580
Would that be possible, Kat?

134
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:18,670
It won't.

135
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:21,670
I only make the things
I want to make.

136
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:22,830
Besides,

137
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:25,210
I've got a birthday order
for the old flour shop lady

138
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:26,460
after the New Year.

139
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:29,630
And I'll prioritize her
over anything else,

140
00:06:29,710 --> 00:06:31,290
the king and the church.

141
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:33,580
Isn't there anything
that you can do?

142
00:06:33,670 --> 00:06:35,080
Without your help, we'll fail!

143
00:06:35,170 --> 00:06:36,750
I already said no, so no!

144
00:06:37,710 --> 00:06:39,210
Say, Mister Kat--

145
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:40,420
- Challe!
- Really?

146
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:41,960
I hate being called
"Mister Kat",

147
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,000
did you forget that?

148
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,080
I remember.

149
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,250
- [ANNE sighs]
- [grunts] That was purposeful?

150
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:49,130
Yes. Purposeful.

151
00:06:49,210 --> 00:06:50,920
You must be looking for a fight!

152
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,830
Wait,
please don't kill each other!

153
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,250
Now then, Mister Kat.

154
00:06:54,630 --> 00:06:56,130
I understand
that you owe a favor

155
00:06:56,210 --> 00:06:57,130
to the Viscount.

156
00:06:57,210 --> 00:06:58,040
[gasps]

157
00:06:58,630 --> 00:07:00,750
[VISCOUNT] I told Kat,
when I talked to you,

158
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:03,330
that you would say something
along those lines.

159
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:04,790
Even then,
he wouldn't back down,

160
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,920
so I decided
we should make it a wager.

161
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:09,080
He bet you'd want me
to get involved,

162
00:07:09,170 --> 00:07:10,420
and I bet you wouldn't.

163
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:11,960
And now that he's lost,

164
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,540
the penalty
is that I have a chance

165
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:15,500
to force him
to do anything I say.

166
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:18,080
Now that you mention it,
that is true.

167
00:07:18,170 --> 00:07:21,080
No, I don't owe a single thing
to that dimwitted reprobate!

168
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:22,830
That was just a joke!

169
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,250
A mere blunder! [grunts]

170
00:07:24,330 --> 00:07:27,080
And that favor,
did he redeem it yet?

171
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:29,380
Well, actually...

172
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:30,920
Is the deal complete?

173
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:32,210
No.

174
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:35,580
Hm?

175
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:38,000
[gasps] That's it!

176
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:40,790
If we can persuade him
to surrender his request,

177
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:43,130
do you think you would be
more willing to help us?

178
00:07:43,210 --> 00:07:45,000
- You can do that?
- Yes!

179
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:47,540
I'm certain he would hand it off
to me instead!

180
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:50,750
Please, I'd be so grateful
if you'd come help us work!

181
00:07:51,250 --> 00:07:52,330
[sighs] I don't know.

182
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:55,000
The Holy Beginnings Festival
isn't only for the royals

183
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:56,330
or the kingdom's religion

184
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:58,460
because it's a time of prayer

185
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:00,830
for the happiness
of all those who live here!

186
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:03,960
And if our confections are good,
we'll have good luck!

187
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:06,420
Which means that we won't have
a bad sugar apple harvest

188
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:07,750
like we did this year!

189
00:08:07,830 --> 00:08:11,170
Hm... Hm...

190
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:15,210
Well, I'd rather do that
than whatever he wants.

191
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:16,670
So yes?

192
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:18,630
Hm.

193
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:21,750
I'll do it!

194
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,130
- [hoofbeats]
- [ANNE] Thank you, Challe!

195
00:08:24,210 --> 00:08:26,580
I'm glad you reminded me
of what Hugh said before!

196
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,710
[CHALLE]
You and Kat are both idiots,

197
00:08:28,790 --> 00:08:30,830
so the conversation
wasn't progressing.

198
00:08:31,250 --> 00:08:32,830
[chuckles]

199
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:34,790
[ANNE]
Even so...

200
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:38,380
it made me really happy that
Challe helped me with something.

201
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:43,500
Oh? There they are!

202
00:08:43,580 --> 00:08:46,040
- [door slams]
- Oh! Great to see you!

203
00:08:47,170 --> 00:08:48,000
Huh?

204
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:50,000
So, what happened with Kat?

205
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:50,920
Hugh!

206
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,170
The right to have Kat
do anything you say,

207
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:54,420
please give it to me!

208
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:57,040
Sorry? [sighs]

209
00:08:57,130 --> 00:08:59,380
I suppose that means
he turned you down, eh?

210
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,960
But he also said that he'd help

211
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:04,250
if I surrendered the right
to that favor.

212
00:09:04,330 --> 00:09:05,330
[gasps]

213
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:06,750
That's exactly right.

214
00:09:06,830 --> 00:09:07,830
So, if you please.

215
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:08,750
I need it!

216
00:09:08,830 --> 00:09:09,830
I refuse.

217
00:09:10,290 --> 00:09:12,500
When Kat creates
a sugar confection,

218
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,420
it's because he actually wants
to do it.

219
00:09:14,830 --> 00:09:17,460
And now, I have a chance
to make him do anything!

220
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:19,920
But Kat is our only hope
to get through this!

221
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:23,040
Well, I have no intention
of spoiling you that much.

222
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:26,040
If you want it that badly,
pry it away from me.

223
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:32,000
Fine, I will.

224
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,170
Really?

225
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:35,500
Are you proposing that we duel?

226
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:38,250
You know,
there are rules about that.

227
00:09:38,330 --> 00:09:40,250
The Silver Sugar Viscount
is only allowed

228
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:42,830
to make confections
that are ordered by the king.

229
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:45,580
That said there is an exception
for contests.

230
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:47,790
[ANNE]
Hm...

231
00:09:51,210 --> 00:09:52,130
[pats]

232
00:09:52,210 --> 00:09:53,040
Huh?

233
00:09:58,210 --> 00:09:59,040
Mm.

234
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:01,920
Let's compete!

235
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,540
[SALIM]
A reckless move.

236
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:06,630
You're kidding.

237
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:08,630
[huffs]

238
00:10:09,290 --> 00:10:10,790
Very well, Halford.

239
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,000
We have a match.

240
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:13,710
You versus me.

241
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:15,880
And the judge?

242
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:18,250
Let me see,

243
00:10:18,330 --> 00:10:19,500
I heard there's a fairy here

244
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:21,290
who's been starving himself
to death.

245
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:25,000
I say whoever manages
to feed him is the winner.

246
00:10:25,710 --> 00:10:27,960
Noah? Hm...

247
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:29,540
All right then!

248
00:10:29,630 --> 00:10:30,670
He'll be the judge!

249
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:32,170
Good!

250
00:10:32,250 --> 00:10:35,040
I'll need my tools
and silver sugar by tomorrow!

251
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:36,830
Bring some for Anne, as well,
Salim!

252
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:37,880
Sir.

253
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,420
Did you hear all that, Collins?

254
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:41,290
I'll be staying here with you.

255
00:10:41,880 --> 00:10:43,500
Make yourself at home then.

256
00:10:44,130 --> 00:10:45,830
Best of luck, Anne.

257
00:10:49,670 --> 00:10:50,830
[MITHRIL]
What?

258
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,750
You versus the Viscount?

259
00:10:52,830 --> 00:10:55,040
He'll mop the floor with you!

260
00:10:55,580 --> 00:10:58,330
[ANNE] Well,
we don't know that for sure.

261
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:00,040
[MITHRIL, ELLIOTT sigh]

262
00:11:00,710 --> 00:11:02,630
Sorry, but it's too much.

263
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,250
Starting work on it today

264
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:06,080
and then feeding it to him
tomorrow?

265
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,040
Pardon me, Anne.

266
00:11:08,130 --> 00:11:09,500
I'm going back
to the hearth now.

267
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:12,420
Can you at least be the one
to tell the others?

268
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:14,460
I'm afraid
I don't have the heart to do it.

269
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:15,380
[whimpers]

270
00:11:16,330 --> 00:11:18,460
[rumbling]

271
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:21,920
[NADIR, VALENTINE grunting]

272
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:25,880
[KING, ORLAND grunting]

273
00:11:27,170 --> 00:11:28,500
[footsteps]

274
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:32,630
[ARTISANS grunting]

275
00:11:32,710 --> 00:11:33,580
Everyone.

276
00:11:34,790 --> 00:11:36,630
Anne! [sighs]

277
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:40,210
Here, put some of this
on your hands!

278
00:11:40,290 --> 00:11:41,830
Your blisters are bursting!

279
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,330
[VALENTINE]
That looks painful!

280
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:48,500
Listen, there's something
I need to tell you.

281
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:50,880
[NADIR]
Oh, we know. Elliott told us.

282
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:52,380
[NADIR, MITHRIL chuckle]

283
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:55,130
Don't worry.
We'll leave it to you.

284
00:11:55,670 --> 00:11:56,500
And in the meantime,

285
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:58,580
we can cover your portion
of the work!

286
00:11:58,670 --> 00:12:00,670
Allow us to handle
everything else, Anne.

287
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,750
You can just concentrate
on winning.

288
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:04,420
Perfectly said!

289
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:06,630
Let's stay strong to the end!
Right?

290
00:12:06,710 --> 00:12:07,670
[NADIR, ORLAND, VALENTINE]
Right!

291
00:12:07,750 --> 00:12:08,580
[gasps]

292
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,250
[ANNE]
This is my job.

293
00:12:10,330 --> 00:12:11,500
I have to succeed!

294
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:15,170
Not just for my own sake,
but for all of theirs, as well!

295
00:12:21,670 --> 00:12:22,500
He's so weak.

296
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,540
I truly hope he'll eat.

297
00:12:25,130 --> 00:12:27,290
He might refuse
to accept either one.

298
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:28,460
I know.

299
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:32,830
But maybe that was why
Hugh suggested this.

300
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,750
He's confident
that he can do it.

301
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,580
Fairies love sugar confections,

302
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:40,000
but does the shape or design
make a difference?

303
00:12:44,170 --> 00:12:47,040
If the shape has special meaning
for you,

304
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:49,830
the fragrance and beauty of it
will be magnified.

305
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:53,380
So, it makes you want
to hold it close

306
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:56,170
much in the same way you long
to kiss someone you love.

307
00:12:56,790 --> 00:12:58,540
[ANNE] I wonder
if there's anything in life

308
00:12:58,630 --> 00:13:01,040
that means as much to Noah
as Lord Herbert does.

309
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:02,880
- [rustle]
- Go to sleep.

310
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:04,460
You'll need all your strength.

311
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:05,380
You too.

312
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,080
I'll watch over him.

313
00:13:07,170 --> 00:13:08,000
But Challe,

314
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,670
you can't stay up
the whole night!

315
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:12,790
Your competition's important.

316
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:14,830
But still... [gasps]

317
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,000
[CHALLE]
What's wrong?

318
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:19,420
Do you need
another goodnight kiss?

319
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:22,500
I'll give you one if I must.

320
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:28,920
Sleep.

321
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:33,540
[ANNE]
Um, good night, Challe!

322
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:37,540
[door creaks and slams]

323
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,170
[SALIM]
Viscount,

324
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:47,170
Anne has arrived
with your breakfast.

325
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:50,670
I see
that you've made a mess again.

326
00:13:51,710 --> 00:13:56,500
- [footsteps]
- [thuds]

327
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:59,670
Haven't I asked you before
to treat books with more care?

328
00:14:00,170 --> 00:14:01,750
And the fathers
who lent them to you,

329
00:14:01,830 --> 00:14:03,710
they had requested
the same thing.

330
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:06,040
I'm the one
who has to return them

331
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:07,330
if you remember.

332
00:14:07,420 --> 00:14:10,170
That isn't what they meant
when they told me to be careful.

333
00:14:10,540 --> 00:14:12,460
They just wanted me
to keep them hidden.

334
00:14:13,130 --> 00:14:14,420
If I weren't in the peerage,

335
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,500
I wouldn't be able to read
any of these.

336
00:14:16,580 --> 00:14:18,670
They're what you would call
"banned books".

337
00:14:19,130 --> 00:14:20,460
Those are banned? Why?

338
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:21,710
What's bad about them?

339
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:25,130
I can't share secrets
with my opponent, now can I?

340
00:14:27,630 --> 00:14:30,080
So, your subject
did you choose one?

341
00:14:30,170 --> 00:14:32,290
Um, well, no.

342
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:34,330
[HUGH]
There's not much time.

343
00:14:35,210 --> 00:14:36,040
[ANNE]
I know.

344
00:14:37,630 --> 00:14:39,040
By the way, Anne,

345
00:14:39,130 --> 00:14:41,750
I have a visit to pay
as soon as breakfast is over.

346
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:44,790
♪

347
00:14:47,540 --> 00:14:49,540
Noah, are you awake now?

348
00:14:50,250 --> 00:14:52,170
There's someone
who'd like a word with you.

349
00:14:53,250 --> 00:14:54,080
[whimpers]

350
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:56,170
[sighs]

351
00:14:56,250 --> 00:14:57,080
[HUGH]
Pardon me.

352
00:14:57,880 --> 00:15:00,460
I'm Silver Sugar Viscount
Hugh Mercury.

353
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:03,170
What?
Oh, I wasn't expecting you, sir.

354
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:05,170
[straining]

355
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:06,380
You can relax.

356
00:15:06,790 --> 00:15:09,000
May I ask you a question, please?

357
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:10,750
Huh?

358
00:15:12,250 --> 00:15:13,630
Your master Herbert,

359
00:15:13,710 --> 00:15:16,750
was he an asset to his house
and a decent man?

360
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:18,420
Yes.

361
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:20,330
I hear he liked
the game of fief.

362
00:15:20,750 --> 00:15:24,330
Hm, well, I shouldn't say this,

363
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:26,790
but truth be told,
he wasn't exactly good at it.

364
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:28,290
Huh?

365
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,670
He was bad at fief, you say?

366
00:15:30,750 --> 00:15:31,580
Right.

367
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:34,080
That's why
he really only ever played it

368
00:15:34,170 --> 00:15:35,000
with me.

369
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:37,250
Hm. I see.

370
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:41,000
Well, that's all, get some rest.

371
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,130
I'll bring you
something nice later

372
00:15:43,210 --> 00:15:44,960
- to say thank you.
- [sighs]

373
00:15:46,250 --> 00:15:48,460
[ANNE] Something
that holds meaning for him.

374
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:49,710
Something he would eat.

375
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,960
If I recreate
Lord Herbert's likeness

376
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:54,880
as a confection,

377
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,080
that might make him happy.

378
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:58,920
Like with the Duke of Philax.

379
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:02,420
But...

380
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:06,580
[footsteps]

381
00:16:06,670 --> 00:16:07,830
[GLADUS]
I hear you're competing

382
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:09,790
- with the Silver Sugar Viscount.
- Huh?

383
00:16:10,420 --> 00:16:12,880
♪

384
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:15,040
- Ah...
- Are you scared?

385
00:16:15,130 --> 00:16:17,080
Is that
because of Challe fenn Challe?

386
00:16:17,170 --> 00:16:18,830
He told you
to stay away from me?

387
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:21,170
Well, that's not exactly it.

388
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:24,460
[gasps]

389
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:27,290
Hm. There's no reason to worry.

390
00:16:28,250 --> 00:16:30,790
I would consider myself
extremely close to him.

391
00:16:31,290 --> 00:16:34,080
But it's impossible
to read his true intentions.

392
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:36,000
I can't get him to open up.

393
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:37,670
You're close?

394
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:39,380
That's right.

395
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,630
And I have no ill intent
toward him

396
00:16:41,710 --> 00:16:44,250
or anything
that he holds precious,

397
00:16:44,330 --> 00:16:46,540
nor do I desire
to do him any harm.

398
00:16:47,670 --> 00:16:48,500
Anne.

399
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,290
- The truth is we two--
- [door slams]

400
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:52,880
What's going on in here?

401
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,330
- [gasps]
- Hm.

402
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:57,210
- [footsteps]
- Nothing at all.

403
00:16:57,830 --> 00:16:59,580
Just having a conversation
with Anne

404
00:16:59,670 --> 00:17:01,960
about her upcoming competition
with the Viscount.

405
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:02,920
Truly?

406
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:04,670
You against him?

407
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:06,790
You're kidding.

408
00:17:07,210 --> 00:17:08,790
It's the only way.

409
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,710
[exhales]

410
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:12,920
[scoffs]
There's no chance you'll win.

411
00:17:13,670 --> 00:17:14,670
So why try?

412
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:16,210
Ah!

413
00:17:17,830 --> 00:17:19,420
We're leaving, Gladus.

414
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:22,210
Right. Take care, Anne.

415
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:26,000
[footsteps]

416
00:17:27,210 --> 00:17:28,250
That was bizarre.

417
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:43,290
[CHALLE] I'm amazed
you're still staring at that.

418
00:17:44,130 --> 00:17:45,540
Have you thought of something?

419
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:49,000
Mm-mm. Not at all.

420
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:52,130
All I can think about
is how bad Noah must feel.

421
00:17:52,710 --> 00:17:55,380
Looking at this old portrait
and missing his master.

422
00:17:55,630 --> 00:17:56,460
Poor thing.

423
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:58,670
[footsteps]

424
00:17:59,330 --> 00:18:01,420
[CHALLE] There must be something
we can't see.

425
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:03,960
Something only Noah is aware of.

426
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,670
[ANNE]
Something we can't see?

427
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:09,330
That's true.

428
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:12,790
If all he wanted to do
was remember the past,

429
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,960
then he wouldn't have to sit
in this spot.

430
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:19,000
There has to be something
about this portrait,

431
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:20,920
but no matter how hard I look...

432
00:18:22,250 --> 00:18:23,830
I'm still not seeing it.

433
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:35,460
♪

434
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:37,500
- [flaps]
- [footsteps]

435
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,080
Say, Challe?

436
00:18:43,670 --> 00:18:45,000
Please take it off the wall,

437
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,830
- would you?
- [CHALLE] Of course.

438
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:49,130
- [thuds]
- [crunching]

439
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,250
Oh...

440
00:18:55,210 --> 00:18:56,040
[gasps]

441
00:18:56,750 --> 00:19:01,710
♪

442
00:19:02,170 --> 00:19:03,080
[CHALLE]
That looks like...

443
00:19:03,670 --> 00:19:06,630
[ANNE] I think
it's the Crest of House Chamber!

444
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:10,080
The royals tried
to destroy them all,

445
00:19:10,170 --> 00:19:11,460
but they missed this one.

446
00:19:12,330 --> 00:19:14,000
And Noah knew it was here.

447
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:16,330
He must've been trying
to guard it.

448
00:19:17,460 --> 00:19:19,750
A crest is the pride
of a noble house,

449
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:21,250
and this is the last one.

450
00:19:21,330 --> 00:19:24,080
It's Lord Herbert's spirit
in physical form.

451
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:26,380
This is what
Noah was looking at!

452
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:28,830
[exhales]

453
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:32,000
Challe,
I know what I'm going to create.

454
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:33,790
Huh?

455
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:35,920
This crest is taboo.

456
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:39,750
The Millsland royal family
erased it from existence.

457
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:42,080
And you plan to resurrect it?

458
00:19:42,630 --> 00:19:43,960
Despite your position?

459
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:46,040
It's risky.

460
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:49,460
As a silver sugar master,
I shouldn't defy the crown.

461
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:52,040
But then what's the harm

462
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:54,130
in people seeing
House Chamber's crest?

463
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:56,710
Everyone who bore it
is gone now.

464
00:19:57,710 --> 00:19:59,210
I'm not making
this sugar confection

465
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:00,380
for the royal family.

466
00:20:01,250 --> 00:20:03,670
I'm making it for the person
who needs it the most.

467
00:20:04,630 --> 00:20:07,630
Because that's what it means
to be a sugar artisan,

468
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:08,750
don't you think so?

469
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:11,960
If there's even one person
who might want it,

470
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:13,670
then that's reason enough!

471
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:16,080
You're bold, aren't you?

472
00:20:16,750 --> 00:20:18,380
Defying the royal family.

473
00:20:18,460 --> 00:20:21,210
I'm not trying
to make people angry,

474
00:20:21,290 --> 00:20:22,960
even if they might think
that I am.

475
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,880
But at this point,
I can't change my mind!

476
00:20:29,210 --> 00:20:30,040
[sighs]

477
00:20:32,630 --> 00:20:35,330
Well, then,
make what you want to make.

478
00:20:37,580 --> 00:20:39,380
- [gasps]
- No matter what comes of it,

479
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:41,290
I will always protect you.

480
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:42,750
And...

481
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:45,130
I'll stay by your side.

482
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:52,210
[clatters]

483
00:20:53,630 --> 00:20:55,920
[water trickling]

484
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,540
[ANNE]
Challe's looking after me.

485
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:38,540
♪

